id: pm-gh1597
title: "GH-1597: expose host-bound item transaction status and safe abandonment or supersession"
description: "GitHub https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1597 requests public recovery for interrupted item-mutation journals when a peer edit changes the retry plan. Existing bulk commit and guarded compensation are shipped; extend their public host-bound lifecycle rather than duplicating private journal storage or reviving completed implementation."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-26T04:54:49.262Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T22:07:24.128Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-28T22:07:22.951Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-28T22:07:22.951Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: Expose typed host-bound journal state and applied/compensated step receipts with plan identity; Provide safe abandonment and supersession using proven apply markers and existing guarded compensation; never overwrite later peer edits or silently compensate committed work; Name executable public recovery in transaction-plan-mismatch guidance and verify non-Git crash/retry/peer-edit controls plus SDK contract documentation
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "Implemented bound status, abandon and supersede APIs with retained original plans, versioned durable retirement intent, idempotent audit and guarded compensation that preserves peer edits. Recovery normalizes identity before markers and can resume retirement after the replacement identity is used. Documented journal retention, redaction scope and the ordinary-writer isolation limit."
expected_result: Packages can inspect and safely retire interrupted item batches through their configured client without rebuilding private journal rules.
actual_result: "65/65 linked recovery tests and full 11540-test exact-coverage run passed; crash, peer-write, padded-identity and replacement-after-crash negative controls verified. Node and Bun packed artifact checks passed. Reviewed delivery is PR #1621; publication remains separate."
