comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T04:54:49.262Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict all-status corpus plus live request-specific searches and full terminal-lineage reads found no exact active owner. Existing SDK promotion and transaction/preview delivery remain completed; this item owns the newly requested public surface."
  "2026-10-28T19:44:07.695Z","harness:codex","Implementation scope: retain original item plans in coordinator journals, expose read-only status and host-bound guarded abandonment/supersession, refuse committed and peer-edited work, preserve append-only compensation and audit evidence. Complete strict 3148-item all-status census has no omissions; 38 open GitHub issues each already have a canonical PM link comment. No open PRs or GitHub dependency/code/secret alerts at intake."
  "2026-10-28T20:16:18.094Z","harness:codex","Native late-peer recovery oracle initially exposed a delete-store gap: the existing scoped item precondition was checked by update/close but not by locked deletion. Isolated candidate adds the same assertion before deletion policy/hooks and centralizes create compensation ownership checks. Close and delete both preserve a peer edit injected immediately before item-lock acquisition. Isolated focused proof passes51 tests; original checkout remains frozen for the in-flight full coverage run. Retirement intent is additionally retained before compensation to fence forward replay across recovery crashes."
  "2026-10-28T20:39:10.736Z","harness:codex","Validation: linked recovery suite passed 65/65, including durable v2 retirement fencing, prepared/applied/recorded crash boundaries, interrupted compensation, audit deduplication, malformed/downgraded receipts and native peer-write races. Typecheck, ESLint, duplicate detection, registry audit and OSV passed. Full canonical coverage is running; no full-coverage success is claimed yet. First complete suite exposed contract snapshot/source-operation registration and preview clock comparison failures, now corrected; its npm package resolution failure was host NODE_PATH configuration, now explicitly set. Published 2026.10.28 verifier passed npm/npx/Bun/bunx and GitHub release checks; this does not imply publication of these branch changes."
  "2026-10-28T21:13:01.117Z","harness:codex","Review remediation: CodeRabbit correctly identified that a durable supersession retry could be permanently blocked if another commit used the chosen replacement id after a crash. The extended final-journal-write interruption regression reproduced the refusal before the fix. Replacement freshness is now checked only when starting retirement; retries retain their original intent and finish without touching the replacement. Added an assertion that plan-mismatch guidance names client.itemTransactions.abandon. Documented journal value retention outside history-redact. Release/telemetry PM observations remain in this grouped delivery because the requested scope explicitly includes these audits; they are not new claims of infrastructure remediation."
  "2026-10-28T21:31:47.832Z","harness:codex","Additional crash regression: a padded transaction id was normalized by the coordinator but not by item-history markers. The extended existing prepared/applied/recorded table proved that applied and recorded attempts could retire while leaving the forward value unchanged. Normalize identity once before building any item step, unique-key index or journal. Local transport admission remains failed; a separately built unchanged base commit also fails all six transport budgets on this host, while the isolated candidate SDK import-cost gate passes. Thresholds are unchanged; exact-head hosted transport admission is required."
  "2026-10-28T21:46:03.949Z","harness:codex","Hosted initial-head evidence: CI job 123098074387 on f705877b712850bb296f8c9ca519848c239d18df passed the SDK import-cost and six-operation CLI transport-floor gates with unchanged budgets. Its static failure was graph-composition prose-edge gaps 1234 > 1233, now corrected by the genuine related edge between the grouped features; local graph and record-integrity gates pass. Bounded mutation evidence is 352 classified mutants, 345 killed, 7 equivalent, no gate failures. Updated packed Node/Bun consumers and unsafe-source rejection passed. Final revised-head hosted checks remain required."
  "2026-10-28T22:07:21.136Z","harness:codex","Final candidate validation: full sandboxed source coverage passed 11540 tests (3 platform skips), 880 passing files and 1 skipped file, with exact 71421/71421 statements, 55025/55025 branches, 14707/14707 functions and 67487/67487 lines. Linked recovery 65/65 and SDK/semantic-preview 49/49 passed, along with typecheck, ESLint, duplicate checks, generated contracts/surface/catalogs, docs links, graph composition and record integrity. Bounded mutation lane: 345 killed and 7 equivalent of 352, no failures. Final packed npm tarball passed Node and Bun batch/replay/retirement/replacement and unsafe-preview bootstrap controls. Local transport performance also failed unchanged base; thresholds remain unchanged and the initial PR head passed both hosted performance gates. Final revised head must pass hosted checks before merge. New APIs are not yet claimed as published."
learnings[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T20:16:19.379Z","harness:codex","Retiring an interrupted batch requires a durable intent before compensation, not only a terminal status afterward. Every destructive compensation must recheck ownership under the target item lock; a pre-lock history comparison alone does not protect a late peer edit."
  "2026-10-28T21:55:42.128Z","harness:codex",Normalize transaction identity before building both durable effects and journal receipts. Normalizing only the coordinator key can make recovery miss its own apply markers and falsely report compensation.
